  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Friday)\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nNoticeably cooler and drier air will arrive for the weekend behind \nthe front, making it feel much more pleasant outside compared to \nthe past several days. Gusty northerly winds will pick up again \nSaturday afternoon as increased flow aloft mixes to the surface \nand wraps around the backside of the departing shortwave. Pleasant\nconditions for early August continue into the beginning of next \nweek before temperatures begin to warm again. The upper ridge is \nprogged to broaden and build back in across much of the southern \nUnited States through the end of next week. A return to near \ntriple digit heat is likely, though dewpoints look to stay a \nlittle lower than they have been through much of July. Rain \nchances look to stay little to none through the rest of the period\nafter this evening.\n\nBowlan",
